#: ../../library/xml.rst:4
msgid "XML Processing Modules"
msgstr "Moduly pro zpracování XML"

#: ../../library/xml.rst:12
msgid "**Source code:** :source:`Lib/xml/`"
msgstr "**Zdrojový kód:** :source:`Lib/xml/`"

#: ../../library/xml.rst:16
msgid ""
"Python's interfaces for processing XML are grouped in the ``xml`` package."
msgstr "Rozhraní Pythonu pro zpracování XML jsou seskupena v balíčku ``xml``."

#: ../../library/xml.rst:20
msgid ""
"If you need to parse untrusted or unauthenticated data, see :ref:`xml-"
"security`."
msgstr ""
"Pokud potřebujete analyzovat nedůvěryhodná nebo neověřená data, podívejte se"
" na :ref:`xml-security`."

#: ../../library/xml.rst:23
msgid ""
"It is important to note that modules in the :mod:`xml` package require that "
"there be at least one SAX-compliant XML parser available. The Expat parser "
"is included with Python, so the :mod:`xml.parsers.expat` module will always "
"be available."
msgstr ""
"Je důležité poznamenat, že moduly v balíčku :mod:`xml` vyžadují přítomnost "
"alespoň jednoho parseru XML kompatibilního se SAX. Parser Expat je součástí "
"Pythonu, takže modul :mod:`xml.parsers.expat` bude vždy k dispozici."

#: ../../library/xml.rst:28
msgid ""
"The documentation for the :mod:`xml.dom` and :mod:`xml.sax` packages are the"
" definition of the Python bindings for the DOM and SAX interfaces."
msgstr ""
"Dokumentace pro balíčky :mod:`xml.dom` a :mod:`xml.sax` jsou definicí "
"Pythonovských vázání rozhraní DOM a SAX."

#: ../../library/xml.rst:31
msgid "The XML handling submodules are:"
msgstr "Podmoduly pro zpracování XML jsou:"

#: ../../library/xml.rst:33
msgid ""
":mod:`xml.etree.ElementTree`: the ElementTree API, a simple and lightweight "
"XML processor"
msgstr ""
":mod:`xml.etree.ElementTree`: API ElementTree, jednoduchý a lehčé XML "
"procesor"

#: ../../library/xml.rst:38
msgid ":mod:`xml.dom`: the DOM API definition"
msgstr ":mod:`xml.dom`: definice API DOM"

#: ../../library/xml.rst:39
msgid ":mod:`xml.dom.minidom`: a minimal DOM implementation"
msgstr ":mod:`xml.dom.minidom`: minimální implementace DOM"

#: ../../library/xml.rst:40
msgid ":mod:`xml.dom.pulldom`: support for building partial DOM trees"
msgstr ":mod:`xml.dom.pulldom`: podpora pro vytváření částných stromů DOM"

#: ../../library/xml.rst:44
msgid ":mod:`xml.sax`: SAX2 base classes and convenience functions"
msgstr ":mod:`xml.sax`: základní třídy SAX2 a funkční pomocniky"

#: ../../library/xml.rst:45
msgid ":mod:`xml.parsers.expat`: the Expat parser binding"
msgstr ":mod:`xml.parsers.expat`: vázání parseru Expat"

#: ../../library/xml.rst:52
msgid "XML security"
msgstr "Bezpečnost XML"

#: ../../library/xml.rst:54
msgid ""
"An attacker can abuse XML features to carry out denial of service attacks, "
"access local files, generate network connections to other machines, or "
"circumvent firewalls when attacker-controlled XML is being parsed, in Python"
" or elsewhere."
msgstr ""
"Utačeř může zneužívat funkce XML k provedení útoků typu denial of service, "
"přístupu k lokálním souborům, generávání sítěových spojení na ostatní "
"počítače nebo obejítí firewallů, pokud je analyzován XML kontrolovaný "
"utačeřem, v Pythonu nebo jinde."

#: ../../library/xml.rst:59
msgid ""
"The built-in XML parsers of Python rely on the library `libexpat`_, commonly"
" called Expat, for parsing XML."
msgstr ""
"Vstavěné XML parsery Pythonu se opírají o knihovnu `libexpat`_, obecně "
"nazývanou Expat, pro analýzu XML."

#: ../../library/xml.rst:62
msgid ""
"By default, Expat itself does not access local files or create network "
"connections."
msgstr ""
"Ve výchozím nastavení Expat sám neprístupušťuje lokálním souborům a nevyčuje"
" sítěová spojení."

#: ../../library/xml.rst:65
msgid ""
"Expat versions lower than 2.7.2 may be vulnerable to the \"billion laughs\","
" \"quadratic blowup\" and \"large tokens\" vulnerabilities, or to "
"disproportional use of dynamic memory. Python bundles a copy of Expat, and "
"whether Python uses the bundled or a system-wide Expat, depends on how the "
"Python interpreter :option:`has been configured <--with-system-expat>` in "
"your environment. Python may be vulnerable if it uses such older versions of"
" Expat. Check :const:`!pyexpat.EXPAT_VERSION`."
msgstr ""
"Verze Expat nižší než 2.7.2 mohou být zranitelný vůči zranělivostem "
"\"billion laughs\", \"quadratic blowup\" a \"large tokens\", nebo vištímu "
"nebalancé mu použíaním dynamické paměti. Python obsahuje kopii Expatu a to, "
"zda Python používá bundled nebo systémově dostupný Expat, závisí na tom, jak"
" je interpret Pythonu :option:`nakonfigurován <--with-system-expat>` ve váem"
" prostředí. Python může být zranitelný, pokud používá takové starší verze "
"Expatu. Zkontrolujte :const:`!pyexpat.EXPAT_VERSION`."

#: ../../library/xml.rst:74
msgid ":mod:`xmlrpc` is **vulnerable** to the \"decompression bomb\" attack."
msgstr ":mod:`xmlrpc` je **zranitelný** vůči útoků \"decompression bomb\"."

#: ../../library/xml.rst:77
msgid "billion laughs / exponential entity expansion"
msgstr "billion laughs / exponenciální expanze entit"

#: ../../library/xml.rst:78
msgid ""
"The `Billion Laughs`_ attack -- also known as exponential entity expansion "
"-- uses multiple levels of nested entities. Each entity refers to another "
"entity several times, and the final entity definition contains a small "
"string. The exponential expansion results in several gigabytes of text and "
"consumes lots of memory and CPU time."
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/xml.rst:84
msgid "quadratic blowup entity expansion"
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/xml.rst:85
msgid ""
"A quadratic blowup attack is similar to a `Billion Laughs`_ attack; it "
"abuses entity expansion, too. Instead of nested entities it repeats one "
"large entity with a couple of thousand chars over and over again. The attack"
" isn't as efficient as the exponential case but it avoids triggering parser "
"countermeasures that forbid deeply nested entities."
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/xml.rst:91
msgid "decompression bomb"
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/xml.rst:92
msgid ""
"Decompression bombs (aka `ZIP bomb`_) apply to all XML libraries that can "
"parse compressed XML streams such as gzipped HTTP streams or LZMA-compressed"
" files. For an attacker it can reduce the amount of transmitted data by "
"three magnitudes or more."
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/xml.rst:98
msgid "large tokens"
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/xml.rst:99
msgid ""
"Expat needs to re-parse unfinished tokens; without the protection introduced"
" in Expat 2.6.0, this can lead to quadratic runtime that can be used to "
"cause denial of service in the application parsing XML. The issue is known "
"as :cve:`2023-52425`."
msgstr ""
